# Module paths & writable files

Resolve paths with **PrestaShop constants**, not relative hops through `dirname(__FILE__)`. Per [PrestaShop good practices](https://devdocs.prestashop-project.org/9/modules/creation/good-practices/): avoid writing generated files inside the module ZIP tree when a shop-level directory exists.

Security-sensitive URL/token rules: `module-security.mdc`. PHP / PS version branching: `module-php.mdc`, `module-prestashop.mdc`.

## Resolve paths with constants

| Need | Constant / pattern |
|---|---|
| Module root on disk | `_PS_MODULE_DIR_ . '<modulename>/'` |
| Module file from main class | `$this->getLocalPath()` when inside `Module` |
| Shop root | `_PS_ROOT_DIR_` |
| Config | `_PS_CONFIG_DIR_` |
| Cache (env-specific) | `_PS_CACHE_DIR_` |

```php
// ❌ BAD — breaks when structure or symlinks differ
require_once dirname(__FILE__) . '/../../config/config.inc.php';

// ✅ GOOD — already bootstrapped in controllers; for requires inside module:
require_once _PS_MODULE_DIR_ . 'cdiscount/classes/cdiscount.tools.class.php';
```

Do not rebuild web URLs by hand when the module already exposes `$this->_path` / `$this->url` — follow existing patterns in that module.

## Where to write generated files

| Kind | Location | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Cache / temp** (exports, locks, progress files) | `_PS_CACHE_DIR_ . '<modulename>/'` | Cleared with shop cache; survives module upgrade |
| **Durable module data** (shared across deploys) | `_PS_ROOT_DIR_ . 'var/modules/<modulename>/'` on PS 8+; on older shops use the same path if `var/modules` exists, else document fallback in the module | Kept when module is uninstalled/reinstalled |
| **Shipped assets** (icons, default XML) | Inside module `views/`, `docs/` | Read-only, part of git |

Avoid growing log/export directories under `/modules/<name>/` on new code — harder in clustered hosting and wiped on naive redeploys.

Create directories with `0755` (or match parent permissions) and check `is_writable` before writing; fail with a clear BO message (see `module-input.mdc`).

## Version note

If `var/modules` is missing on an old 1.7 shop, follow the fallback already used in that module's codebase — do not introduce a third pattern.

## Never

- `dirname(__FILE__) . '/../../…'` to reach `config.inc.php` or core files.
- Assume `getcwd()` or `$_SERVER['DOCUMENT_ROOT']` for module paths.
- Write cache/temp files next to PHP sources under `classes/` or `controllers/`.
